    "narrative": "For the May 31st slate, our offensive engine is anchored by **Jose Caballero**, who sits atop our efficiency rankings with a massive 80.26 score. He benefits from a rare combination of a favorable park factor (+10%) and an advantageous platoon split against the southpaw Lopez, making him our primary engine for the scarce Stolen Base category. **Corbin Carroll** (73.68) and **Brice Turang** (71.97) follow closely behind; while **Corbin Carroll** faces a decent arm in Miller, his elite speed and top-of-the-order positioning make him a near-lock for production, and **Brice Turang** draws a significant boost (+19% SP Skill) from a matchup against Imai, whose xERA of 5.17 suggests a high likelihood of a multi-hit game.\n\nThe decision to bench **Austin Riley** (51.66) was the most difficult call of the morning. While he maintains high power potential, his matchup against the difficult Lodolo (3.83 xERA) created a performance ceiling that couldn't compete with the efficiency scores of our middle-of-the-order bats like **Josh Naylor** (66.01) or **Kyle Karros** (62.24). **Kyle Karros** specifically represents a high-upside play today, as the combination of park factors (+14%) and platoon advantage (+7%) provides a significantly safer floor than **Austin Riley**\u2019s difficult left-on-left scenario. \n\nRegarding risks, we are monitoring the bottom of our lineup carefully. Both **Dalton Rushing** (51.56) and **Alex Freeland** (46.95) are starting despite lower efficiency scores, primarily due to their roles in our depth chart against the right-handed Painter. While **Dalton Rushing** provides value through his elite defensive framing and catching floor, his position at #8 in the order drags his score down by 6%. Similarly, **Alex Freeland** at #9 creates a bottleneck in lineup production. We have ruled out **Mickey Moniak** entirely as he remains on the IL, while **Zach McKinstry** and **Travis Bazzana** remain relegated to the bench as they fail to clear the 50-point threshold required to displace our current starters against their respective opposing arms.",
